// The package replica is the design model of the sync replica
// (examples/lease-sync/replica): optimistic mutation, rebase by rerun of
// decide, push and pull over a bad network, a client restart that loses the
// cache, and the screen. It is checked by `ergo test models/replica` (the
// explorer: a breadth-first search of every state in a small scope; the
// gate's full tier). It replaced a Quint model of the 2026-11 sync spike, a
// random simulation.
//
// One authority keeps a log of receipts (who, id, command, applied). It
// reruns decide on its own state: a resend of an id with a receipt is a
// no-op, an id past the client's next one is refused, and a command the
// state does not allow gets a refused receipt (the refusal is recorded, so a
// client's ids have no hole). Each client keeps a base (the replay of the
// log prefix it has read), a cursor, a queue of pending mutations, the next
// id, the floor and the refusals it was told (Told, the Refused list of the
// client state); its view is the base plus a rerun of the pending
// mutations. The journal keeps the queue, the next id, the floor and Told; a
// restart loses the base and the cursor. The floor is the cursor at the
// last prune of the queue: until the cursor is at the floor again the
// replica is Loading. Each commit of a replica posts its view to the host
// queue; the main thread takes a post and shows it.
//
// Frames. A delta carries the log entries from a position; a snapshot
// carries the state at a position, the caller's last id at it (LastSeq),
// and the caller's refused commands in the range it skips (Refused). A
// snapshot without the refusals prunes a refused command from the queue and
// the client never learns its typed reason (mutant 13).
//
// The domain is a counter: Reserve needs a free unit, Release needs a taken
// one, so the authority can refuse what a client predicted.
//
// The network, and why the model holds no message. A delivery is one
// action, and the merge is exact for the design:
//   - Deliver{C, I} gives the authority the I-th pending mutation of C. A
//     mutation leaves the queue only when its receipt is in the log prefix
//     the client has read, so a late copy of a mutation that is no longer
//     pending is a resend of an id with a receipt: a no-op. A copy that is
//     still pending can be delivered now. So every delivery of an in-flight
//     copy is this action or a no-op: duplicates (the action again),
//     reorders (I = 1 before I = 0, refused as ahead) and loss (never).
//   - Delta{C, From, To} and Snapshot{C, At} are a frame the authority
//     makes from any position and the client takes at once. The log only
//     grows, so a frame made earlier and delivered now is a frame that can
//     be made now: old, doubled and reordered frames are these actions.
//   - A link that is down (Link{C}) stops both for C: a partition.
//
// The screen. Posts is the host queue of a client, oldest first. Render
// takes any post. The design shows it only if it is of the current
// instance (epoch), and drops it and every older post (the rule "newer
// than the one shown", since every post behind it in the queue is older).
// A restart ends the instance: its posts can never show, so the design
// drops them at the restart (exact: a dead post changes nothing but the
// length of the queue). The queue holds QueueCap posts; one more drops the
// oldest, which the design allows (the host may skip to a later state).
// This bound is part of the scope.
//
// Each action is a signal; an action that is not enabled is Ignore. The
// invariants are checked after each step: a step that breaks one enters
// Broken with its name.
//
//   - FreeInRange, StateIsLogReplay, ReceiptsContiguous: the authority's
//     state is legal and is the replay of its log; each client's receipts
//     are ids 1, 2, ... once each (exactly once);
//   - NoLostMutation: every mutation a client issued has its one receipt or
//     still waits in the queue;
//   - BaseIsPrefixReplay: a replica's base is the replay of the log prefix
//     it has read;
//   - ViewCommittedPlusPending, ShownCommittedPlusPending: a Ready view, and
//     what the screen shows, is the authority's state at one log position
//     plus the client's own pending tail, in order, with no gap, none twice;
//   - NoStaleShown: the screen shows only the current replica instance;
//   - ReadyIsStable: a Ready replica stays Ready until a restart;
//   - SettledShowsLatest: when the host queue is empty the screen is the
//     replica's view;
//   - QuiescentConvergence, SettledScreensAgree: when every queue is empty
//     and every replica has read the whole log, every view, and every
//     settled screen, is the authority's state;
//   - RefusalIsTold: a client knows the refusal of each of its commands
//     that the log prefix it has read holds as refused.
//
// The scope: 1 unit; client A issues up to 2 mutations and B up to 1 (so a
// log of up to 3 receipts); A restarts up to once; a host queue of 2. It is
// the claim: "proved" means proved in this scope (459,364 states). A larger
// scope is opt-in: in a copy of this file set MaxRestartsB = 1 (B also
// restarts once; 1,743,732 states) or Seats = 2, and run
// `ergo test <copy> --law Design.Safe --states 4000000`.
//
// Mutants, each a machine whose law Breaks must hold: a shortest run that
// breaks the invariant the fault is planted to break (a run that breaks
// another invariant first ends in Other and is not counted):
//    1 ApplyResend: the authority applies a resend again (ReceiptsContiguous);
//    2 TrustClient: the authority trusts the client's prediction (FreeInRange);
//    3 KeepConfirmed: a confirmed mutation stays pending after a delta
//      (ViewCommittedPlusPending);
//    4 SnapshotNoLastID: a snapshot carries no last mutation id
//      (ViewCommittedPlusPending);
//    5 AcceptGap: a delta past the cursor is applied (BaseIsPrefixReplay);
//    6 AcceptOldSnapshot: a snapshot behind the cursor is applied
//      (ReadyIsStable);
//    7 NoFloor: a restarted replica is Ready before its floor
//      (ViewCommittedPlusPending);
//    8 IDsNotJournaled: a restart derives the next id from the queue
//      (NoLostMutation);
//    9 DropOnUnlink: a dropped link clears the queue (NoLostMutation);
//   10 NoEpochCheck: the screen takes a post of an old instance
//      (NoStaleShown);
//   11 NoOrderCheck: the screen takes an older post after a newer one
//      (SettledShowsLatest);
//   12 RefusalChangesState: a refused command still changes the authority's
//      state (StateIsLogReplay);
//   13 SnapshotDropsRefusals: a snapshot carries LastSeq and no refusal, so
//      a refused command it skips leaves the queue untold (RefusalIsTold).
// QuiescentConvergence, SettledScreensAgree and ShownCommittedPlusPending
// have no mutant of their own: in the design they follow from the other
// invariants, and they are stated because they are the properties a user
// sees.
//
// Witnesses, the `sometimes` laws of Design, so the invariants are not
// vacuous: convergence after a refusal; convergence over the full log of 3
// receipts with every screen settled; a replica that was Loading after a
// restart and is Ready again with a mutation pending; a restarted replica
// still Loading; convergence after a refusal and a Loading restart in one
// run; a partition that holds a full queue while other work lands.

type Who = A{} | B{}

type Cmd = Reserve{} | Release{}

type Mutation { By Who, ID int, Cmd Cmd }

type Entry { By Who, ID int, Cmd Cmd, Applied bool }

// View is what a replica shows: Loading (Ready false), or the base at log
// position K plus a rerun of the pending mutations Muts.
type View { Ready bool, K int, Muts []Mutation, Value int }

type Post { Epoch int, View View }

type Client {
	// The cache, lost at a restart.
	Base   int,
	Cursor int,
	// The journal, kept at a restart.
	Pending []Mutation,
	NextID  int,
	Floor   int,
	// Told is the ids of this client's commands that it was told are
	// refused: the model of the client state's Refused list.
	Told []int,
	// The connection and the instance.
	Linked bool,
	Epoch  int,
	// Ghosts, read only by the invariants.
	Issued     []Mutation,
	WasReady   bool,
	WasLoading bool,
	// The host queue and the screen.
	Posts      []Post,
	ShownEpoch int,
	Shown      View,
}

type World { Log []Entry, Free int, A Client, B Client }

// St is the model's state: the world, a broken invariant, or (in a mutant
// machine) another invariant broken first.
type St = Live{W World} | Broken{Why string} | Other{Why string}

// Slot is an index into a client's pending queue or host queue.
type Slot = I0{} | I1{}

// Pos is a log position.
type Pos = P0{} | P1{} | P2{} | P3{}

type Act = Mutate{C Who, Cmd Cmd} | Deliver{C Who, I Slot} | Delta{C Who, From Pos, To Pos} | Snapshot{C Who, At Pos} | Link{C Who} | Restart{C Who} | Render{C Who, I Slot}

// The scope.
let Seats = 1
let MaxMutsA = 2
let MaxMutsB = 1
let MaxRestartsA = 1
let MaxRestartsB = 0
let QueueCap = 2

// The mutants and the design, as the argument of next.
let NoMutant = 0
let ApplyResend = 1
let TrustClient = 2
let KeepConfirmed = 3
let SnapshotNoLastID = 4
let AcceptGap = 5
let AcceptOldSnapshot = 6
let NoFloor = 7
let IDsNotJournaled = 8
let DropOnUnlink = 9
let NoEpochCheck = 10
let NoOrderCheck = 11
let RefusalChangesState = 12
let SnapshotDropsRefusals = 13

func loading() View { View{Ready: false, K: 0, Muts: []Mutation{}, Value: 0} }

func fresh() Client {
	Client{
		Base:       Seats,
		Cursor:     0,
		Pending:    []Mutation{},
		NextID:     1,
		Floor:      0,
		Told:       []int{},
		Linked:     true,
		Epoch:      0,
		Issued:     []Mutation{},
		WasReady:   true,
		WasLoading: false,
		Posts:      []Post{},
		ShownEpoch: 0,
		Shown:      View{Ready: true, K: 0, Muts: []Mutation{}, Value: Seats},
	}
}

func first() St { Live{W: World{Log: []Entry{}, Free: Seats, A: fresh(), B: fresh()}} }

func slot(i Slot) int {
	match i {
	case I0:
		0
	case I1:
		1
	}
}

func pos(p Pos) int {
	match p {
	case P0:
		0
	case P1:
		1
	case P2:
		2
	case P3:
		3
	}
}

func get(w World, c Who) Client {
	match c {
	case A:
		w.A
	case B:
		w.B
	}
}

func set(w World, c Who, v Client) World {
	match c {
	case A:
		World{..w, A: v}
	case B:
		World{..w, B: v}
	}
}

func maxMuts(c Who) int {
	match c {
	case A:
		MaxMutsA
	case B:
		MaxMutsB
	}
}

func maxRestarts(c Who) int {
	match c {
	case A:
		MaxRestartsA
	case B:
		MaxRestartsB
	}
}

// The domain: decide, then evolve.
func decide(f int, c Cmd) bool {
	match c {
	case Reserve:
		f > 0
	case Release:
		f < Seats
	}
}

func evolve(f int, c Cmd) int {
	match c {
	case Reserve:
		f - 1
	case Release:
		f + 1
	}
}

// replay is f after the applied entries of log at positions from up to to.
func replay(log []Entry, from int, to int, f int) int {
	let mut out = f
	for i, e in log {
		if i >= from && i < to && e.Applied {
			out = evolve(out, e.Cmd)
		}
	}
	out
}

// rerun is f after the pending mutations: each is decided on the state the
// one before it left.
func rerun(ms []Mutation, f int) int {
	let mut out = f
	for m in ms {
		if decide(out, m.Cmd) {
			out = evolve(out, m.Cmd)
		}
	}
	out
}

// lastID is the highest id of c among the first upto entries of log.
func lastID(log []Entry, upto int, c Who) int {
	let mut out = 0
	for i, e in log {
		if i < upto && e.By == c && e.ID > out {
			out = e.ID
		}
	}
	out
}

// push is the authority's step for the mutation mu.
func push(m int, w World, mu Mutation) World {
	let last = lastID(w.Log, len(w.Log), mu.By)
	if m != ApplyResend && mu.ID <= last {
		return w
	}
	if mu.ID > last+1 {
		return w
	}
	let ok = m == TrustClient || decide(w.Free, mu.Cmd)
	World{..w,
		Log:  w.Log.Append(Entry{By: mu.By, ID: mu.ID, Cmd: mu.Cmd, Applied: ok}),
		Free: if ok || m == RefusalChangesState { evolve(w.Free, mu.Cmd) } else { w.Free },
	}
}

func viewOf(c Client) View {
	if c.Cursor >= c.Floor {
		View{Ready: true, K: c.Cursor, Muts: c.Pending, Value: rerun(c.Pending, c.Base)}
	} else {
		loading()
	}
}

// commit is c after one commit of the replica: its view joins the host
// queue, and the oldest post leaves a full queue.
func commit(c Client) Client {
	let v = viewOf(c)
	let all = c.Posts.Append(Post{Epoch: c.Epoch, View: v})
	let mut kept = []Post{}
	for i, p in all {
		if len(all)-i <= QueueCap {
			kept = kept.Append(p)
		}
	}
	Client{..c, WasReady: c.WasReady || v.Ready, WasLoading: c.WasLoading || !v.Ready, Posts: kept}
}

func above(ms []Mutation, id int) []Mutation {
	let mut out = []Mutation{}
	for m in ms {
		if m.ID > id {
			out = out.Append(m)
		}
	}
	out
}

func highest(ms []Mutation) int {
	let mut out = 0
	for m in ms {
		if m.ID > out {
			out = m.ID
		}
	}
	out
}

// applied is me after it takes a frame that moves the cursor to to with
// the base base; prune says whether the frame tells the client which of its
// mutations the log holds.
func applied(w World, c Who, me Client, base int, to int, prune bool, tell bool) Client {
	let known = lastID(w.Log, to, c)
	commit(Client{..me,
		Base:    base,
		Cursor:  to,
		Pending: if prune { above(me.Pending, known) } else { me.Pending },
		Floor:   if me.Floor > to { me.Floor } else { to },
		Told:    if tell { told(w.Log, to, c, me.Told) } else { me.Told },
	})
}

func has(xs []int, x int) bool {
	for y in xs {
		if y == x {
			return true
		}
	}
	false
}

// told is have plus the ids of c's refused commands among the first upto
// entries of log: what a frame that carries the caller's refusals tells.
func told(log []Entry, upto int, c Who, have []int) []int {
	let mut out = have
	for i, e in log {
		if i < upto && e.By == c && !e.Applied && !has(out, e.ID) {
			out = out.Append(e.ID)
		}
	}
	out
}

// refusalIsTold says that c knows the refusal of each of its commands that
// the log prefix it has read holds as refused.
func refusalIsTold(w World, c Who) bool {
	let me = get(w, c)
	for i, e in w.Log {
		if i < me.Cursor && e.By == c && !e.Applied && !has(me.Told, e.ID) {
			return false
		}
	}
	true
}

// next is w after the action a under the mutant m (NoMutant is the design),
// or None when a is not enabled.
func next(m int, w World, a Act) Option[World] {
	match a {
	case Mutate as x:
		// A press: the mutation joins the queue and the journal, and the
		// view shows it at once.
		let me = get(w, x.C)
		if len(me.Issued) >= maxMuts(x.C) {
			return None
		}
		let mu = Mutation{By: x.C, ID: me.NextID, Cmd: x.Cmd}
		Some[World]{Value: set(w, x.C, commit(Client{..me,
			Pending: me.Pending.Append(mu),
			NextID:  me.NextID + 1,
			Issued:  me.Issued.Append(mu),
		}))}
	case Deliver as x:
		// The network gives the authority a pending mutation of C.
		let me = get(w, x.C)
		let i = slot(x.I)
		if !me.Linked || i >= len(me.Pending) {
			return None
		}
		let w2 = push(m, w, me.Pending[i])
		if w2 == w {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: w2}
	case Delta as x:
		// The client takes the log entries from From up to To. The design
		// takes them only when they join the cursor and bring something new.
		let me = get(w, x.C)
		let from = pos(x.From)
		let to = pos(x.To)
		if !me.Linked || from > to || to > len(w.Log) || to <= me.Cursor {
			return None
		}
		if from > me.Cursor && m != AcceptGap {
			return None
		}
		let start = if from > me.Cursor { from } else { me.Cursor }
		Some[World]{Value: set(w, x.C, applied(w, x.C, me, replay(w.Log, start, to, me.Base), to, m != KeepConfirmed, true))}
	case Snapshot as x:
		// The client takes the state at At. The design takes it only when
		// it is past the cursor.
		let me = get(w, x.C)
		let at = pos(x.At)
		if !me.Linked || at > len(w.Log) {
			return None
		}
		if at <= me.Cursor && (m != AcceptOldSnapshot || at == me.Cursor) {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: set(w, x.C, applied(w, x.C, me, replay(w.Log, 0, at, Seats), at, m != SnapshotNoLastID, m != SnapshotDropsRefusals))}
	case Link as x:
		// A partition starts or ends. The queue stays.
		let me = get(w, x.C)
		if m == DropOnUnlink && me.Linked && len(me.Pending) > 0 {
			return Some[World]{Value: set(w, x.C, commit(Client{..me, Linked: false, Pending: []Mutation{}}))}
		}
		Some[World]{Value: set(w, x.C, Client{..me, Linked: !me.Linked})}
	case Restart as x:
		// The program stops and starts again: a new instance reads the
		// journal, the cache is gone, and the screen shows Loading.
		let me = get(w, x.C)
		if me.Epoch >= maxRestarts(x.C) {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: set(w, x.C, commit(Client{..me,
			Base:       Seats,
			Cursor:     0,
			NextID:     if m == IDsNotJournaled { highest(me.Pending) + 1 } else { me.NextID },
			Floor:      if m == NoFloor { 0 } else { me.Floor },
			Epoch:      me.Epoch + 1,
			WasReady:   false,
			Posts:      if m == NoEpochCheck { me.Posts } else { []Post{} },
			ShownEpoch: me.Epoch + 1,
			Shown:      loading(),
		}))}
	case Render as x:
		// The main thread takes one post from the host queue.
		let me = get(w, x.C)
		let i = slot(x.I)
		if i >= len(me.Posts) {
			return None
		}
		let p = me.Posts[i]
		let mut rest = []Post{}
		for j, q in me.Posts {
			if j > i || (m == NoOrderCheck && j < i) {
				rest = rest.Append(q)
			}
		}
		Some[World]{Value: set(w, x.C, Client{..me, Posts: rest, ShownEpoch: p.Epoch, Shown: p.View})}
	}
}

// The invariants.

func count(ms []Mutation, m Mutation) int {
	let mut n = 0
	for x in ms {
		if x == m {
			n = n + 1
		}
	}
	n
}

func receiptsContiguous(w World, c Who) bool {
	let mut want = 1
	for e in w.Log {
		if e.By == c {
			if e.ID != want {
				return false
			}
			want = want + 1
		}
	}
	true
}

func noLostMutation(w World, c Who) bool {
	let me = get(w, c)
	let last = lastID(w.Log, len(w.Log), c)
	let waiting = above(me.Pending, last)
	let mut mine = 0
	for e in w.Log {
		if e.By == c {
			mine = mine + 1
		}
	}
	if len(me.Issued) != mine+len(waiting) {
		return false
	}
	for mu in me.Issued {
		let mut receipts = 0
		for e in w.Log {
			if e.By == c && e.ID == mu.ID && e.Cmd == mu.Cmd {
				receipts = receipts + 1
			}
		}
		if receipts != 1 && count(waiting, mu) != 1 {
			return false
		}
	}
	true
}

// committedPlusPending says that a Ready view of c is the authority's state
// at the log position v.K plus c's own mutations with no receipt at v.K.
func committedPlusPending(w World, c Who, v View) bool {
	if !v.Ready {
		return true
	}
	let last = lastID(w.Log, v.K, c)
	for i, mu in v.Muts {
		if mu.ID != last+1+i || count(get(w, c).Issued, mu) != 1 {
			return false
		}
	}
	v.Value == rerun(v.Muts, replay(w.Log, 0, v.K, Seats))
}

func quiescent(w World) bool {
	len(w.A.Pending) == 0 && len(w.B.Pending) == 0 && w.A.Cursor == len(w.Log) && w.B.Cursor == len(w.Log)
}

func settled(w World) bool { len(w.A.Posts) == 0 && len(w.B.Posts) == 0 }

func showsFree(w World, v View) bool { v.Ready && v.Value == w.Free }

// holdsFor is the invariant name for the client c.
func holdsFor(name string, w World, c Who) bool {
	let me = get(w, c)
	if name == "ReceiptsContiguous" {
		return receiptsContiguous(w, c)
	}
	if name == "NoLostMutation" {
		return noLostMutation(w, c)
	}
	if name == "BaseIsPrefixReplay" {
		return me.Base == replay(w.Log, 0, me.Cursor, Seats)
	}
	if name == "ViewCommittedPlusPending" {
		return committedPlusPending(w, c, viewOf(me))
	}
	if name == "ShownCommittedPlusPending" {
		return committedPlusPending(w, c, me.Shown)
	}
	if name == "NoStaleShown" {
		return me.ShownEpoch == me.Epoch
	}
	if name == "ReadyIsStable" {
		return !me.WasReady || viewOf(me).Ready
	}
	if name == "SettledShowsLatest" {
		return len(me.Posts) != 0 || me.Shown == viewOf(me)
	}
	if name == "QuiescentConvergence" {
		return !quiescent(w) || showsFree(w, viewOf(me))
	}
	if name == "RefusalIsTold" {
		return refusalIsTold(w, c)
	}
	if name == "SettledScreensAgree" {
		return !(quiescent(w) && settled(w)) || showsFree(w, me.Shown)
	}
	true
}

// holds is the invariant name in w.
func holds(name string, w World) bool {
	if name == "FreeInRange" {
		return w.Free >= 0 && w.Free <= Seats
	}
	if name == "StateIsLogReplay" {
		return replay(w.Log, 0, len(w.Log), Seats) == w.Free
	}
	holdsFor(name, w, A) && holdsFor(name, w, B)
}

func names() []string {
	[]string{
		"FreeInRange", "StateIsLogReplay", "ReceiptsContiguous", "NoLostMutation", "BaseIsPrefixReplay",
		"ViewCommittedPlusPending", "ShownCommittedPlusPending", "NoStaleShown", "ReadyIsStable",
		"SettledShowsLatest", "QuiescentConvergence", "SettledScreensAgree", "RefusalIsTold",
	}
}

// broken is the name of the first invariant w breaks, or "".
func broken(w World) string {
	for n in names() {
		if !holds(n, w) {
			return n
		}
	}
	""
}

// stepWith is the step under the mutant m. The design (want "") enters
// Broken at any broken invariant. A mutant enters Broken only when the
// invariant want breaks, and Other when another one breaks first.
func stepWith(m int, want string, s St, a Act) Decision[St, string] {
	match s {
	case Live as l:
		match next(m, l.W, a) {
		case None:
			Ignore
		case Some[World] as n:
			if want != "" && !holds(want, n.Value) {
				return Enter[St]{Next: Broken{Why: want}}
			}
			let why = broken(n.Value)
			if why == "" {
				Enter[St]{Next: Live{W: n.Value}}
			} else if want == "" {
				Enter[St]{Next: Broken{Why: why}}
			} else {
				Enter[St]{Next: Other{Why: why}}
			}
		}
	case _:
		Ignore
	}
}

func stepDesign(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string]            { stepWith(NoMutant, "", s, a) }
func stepApplyResend(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string]       { stepWith(ApplyResend, "ReceiptsContiguous", s, a) }
func stepTrustClient(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string]       { stepWith(TrustClient, "FreeInRange", s, a) }
func stepKeepConfirmed(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string]     { stepWith(KeepConfirmed, "ViewCommittedPlusPending", s, a) }
func stepSnapshotNoLastID(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string]  { stepWith(SnapshotNoLastID, "ViewCommittedPlusPending", s, a) }
func stepAcceptGap(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string]         { stepWith(AcceptGap, "BaseIsPrefixReplay", s, a) }
func stepAcceptOldSnapshot(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string] { stepWith(AcceptOldSnapshot, "ReadyIsStable", s, a) }
func stepNoFloor(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string]           { stepWith(NoFloor, "ViewCommittedPlusPending", s, a) }
func stepIDsNotJournaled(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string]   { stepWith(IDsNotJournaled, "NoLostMutation", s, a) }
func stepDropOnUnlink(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string]      { stepWith(DropOnUnlink, "NoLostMutation", s, a) }
func stepNoEpochCheck(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string]      { stepWith(NoEpochCheck, "NoStaleShown", s, a) }
func stepNoOrderCheck(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string]      { stepWith(NoOrderCheck, "SettledShowsLatest", s, a) }
func stepRefusalChangesState(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string] {
	stepWith(RefusalChangesState, "StateIsLogReplay", s, a)
}

func stepSnapshotDropsRefusals(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string] {
	stepWith(SnapshotDropsRefusals, "RefusalIsTold", s, a)
}

// The witnesses, as predicates on the state.

func refused(w World) bool {
	for e in w.Log {
		if !e.Applied {
			return true
		}
	}
	false
}

func convergedAfterRefusal(s St) bool {
	match s {
	case Live as l:
		quiescent(l.W) && settled(l.W) && refused(l.W)
	case _:
		false
	}
}

func convergedOverFullLog(s St) bool {
	match s {
	case Live as l:
		quiescent(l.W) && settled(l.W) && len(l.W.Log) == MaxMutsA+MaxMutsB
	case _:
		false
	}
}

func restartedReadyWithPending(s St) bool {
	match s {
	case Live as l:
		l.W.A.WasLoading && viewOf(l.W.A).Ready && len(l.W.A.Pending) > 0
	case _:
		false
	}
}

func convergedAfterRefusalAndRestart(s St) bool {
	match s {
	case Live as l:
		quiescent(l.W) && settled(l.W) && refused(l.W) && l.W.A.WasLoading
	case _:
		false
	}
}

func heldWhileUnlinked(s St) bool {
	match s {
	case Live as l:
		!l.W.A.Linked && len(l.W.A.Pending) == MaxMutsA && len(l.W.Log) > 0
	case _:
		false
	}
}

func restartedStillLoading(s St) bool {
	match s {
	case Live as l:
		l.W.A.Epoch > 0 && !viewOf(l.W.A).Ready
	case _:
		false
	}
}

// The design keeps every invariant in the scope.
type Design machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepDesign,

	law Safe never reaches Broken,
	law ConvergesAfterRefusal sometimes convergedAfterRefusal,
	law ConvergesOverFullLog sometimes convergedOverFullLog,
	law RestartsReadyWithPending sometimes restartedReadyWithPending,
	law RestartsLoading sometimes restartedStillLoading,
	law ConvergesAfterRefusalAndRestart sometimes convergedAfterRefusalAndRestart,
	law HoldsWhileUnlinked sometimes heldWhileUnlinked,
}

type MutantApplyResend machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepApplyResend,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

type MutantTrustClient machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepTrustClient,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

type MutantKeepConfirmed machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepKeepConfirmed,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

type MutantSnapshotNoLastID machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepSnapshotNoLastID,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

type MutantAcceptGap machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepAcceptGap,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

type MutantAcceptOldSnapshot machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepAcceptOldSnapshot,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

type MutantNoFloor machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepNoFloor,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

type MutantIDsNotJournaled machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepIDsNotJournaled,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

type MutantDropOnUnlink machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepDropOnUnlink,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

type MutantNoEpochCheck machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepNoEpochCheck,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

type MutantNoOrderCheck machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepNoOrderCheck,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

type MutantRefusalChangesState machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepRefusalChangesState,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}

// MutantSnapshotDropsRefusals is the frame Snapshot{At, State, LastSeq}
// with no refusals: a client that passes a refused command of its own by a
// snapshot prunes it from Pending and never learns that it was refused.
type MutantSnapshotDropsRefusals machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepSnapshotDropsRefusals,

	law Breaks reaches Broken,
}
